{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems","id":1489575,"title":"VtM But in Different Systems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-09T12:17:12-07:00","id":1489575,"title":"VtM But in Different Systems","content":"I came across a GURPS version of VtM a while back and that got me to wondering. Have any of you taken the setting from VtM and used a different game system for it?<br /> <br /> If so, which ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 08-09-2022, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T12:33:49-07:00","id":1489577,"title":"","content":"GURPS Vampire has a pretty cool version of New Orleans with Robert Johnson as the Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T12:40:42-07:00","id":1489578,"title":"","content":"I can dig that. A toreador?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T20:26:47-07:00","id":1489602,"title":"","content":"In a very, very weird game, I've got to adapt WoD to TormentaRPG, a Brazillian D&amp;D 3.X. While the final result wasn't stellar, since then I do intent on making a full adaptation for D&amp;D 3.5 and/or 5th ed (I don't know 4th enough to try and my players wouldn't touch it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T21:00:29-07:00","id":1489607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1489602#post1489602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a very, very weird game, I've got to adapt WoD to TormentaRPG, a Brazillian D&amp;D 3.X. While the final result wasn't stellar, since then I do intent on making a full adaptation for D&amp;D 3.5 and/or 5th ed (I don't know 4th enough to try and my players wouldn't touch it).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool. I can appreciate that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T09:35:03-07:00","id":1489749,"title":"","content":"I know there was a d20 system by Monte Cook for &quot;world of darkness&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T11:00:58-07:00","id":1489762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1489749#post1489749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there was a d20 system by Monte Cook for &quot;world of darkness&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do remember skimming though that. What was his particular rendition. Kind of like &quot;Stan Lee creates the DC Universe.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T13:26:13-07:00","id":1489781,"title":"","content":"VtM 4th Edition by OPP was going to run on something similar to the Storypath system....the conversion is pretty easy and it runs well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T13:40:24-07:00","id":1489783,"title":"","content":"There was one time my group tried converting V:tM to use the Lone Wolf Multiplayer system. This was a simple RPG system by Mongoose Publishing extrapolated from the Lone Wolf choose your own adventure books by Joe Dever.<br /> <br /> The LWM system basically runs off a single D10, a combat chart, a combat skill base number, and an Endurance score (hit points). Rather than having XP you just gain one new ability after an adventure. Rather than seeing if you make a roll or not, if you have the stats, you succeed. But if you don't have the stats, you fail. The ST adjusts the outcome accordingly, though may have you do a roll occasionally.<br /> <br /> On the plus side this made combats so much less of a slog to get through. Rather than figuring out difficulty or number of actions or armor soak, you just take your base Combat Skill and adjust it with any applicable modifiers and compare the adjusted CS number to the opponents adjusted number on the combat chart and roll a single D10, the roll is then looked up on the chart with the results all precalculated.<br /> <br /> The downside is that if you really were invested in the mechanical crunch of the D10 system, this meant your build got boiled down to a very simplified form. Rather than geeking out to Celerity giving you X number of additional actions, it just gave you say a +2 on your Combat Skill and in narrative moments would give you different options considering how fast you could move.<br /> <br /> One interesting thing is that drove home the vampire angle with this system is that there wasn't a Blood Pool per se. Your Endurance Score which functioned as your health levels pulled double duty as your Blood Pool to activate the most powerful of abilities. Thus to using your best powers was a double edged sword, and to heal you had to feed.<br /> <br /> It was fun to play with and in my opinion gave more of a sense of progression than most Storyteller system games, but it was a system that needed far more refinement to make a full port of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T13:57:15-07:00","id":1489784,"title":"","content":"GURPS VtM is for Gurps 3e. Since I much rather prefer Gurps 4e, I have adapted it for the 4e.<br /> <br /> Since Gurps 4e also allows for a lot more flexibilization, I nuked a lot of things from VtM, in particular the Disciplines mechanics. I use the system of powers for Gurps to design their &quot;disciplines&quot;, and in my modest opinion, it's a huge improvement. The powers now are much more balanced and much better suitable for &quot;uniqueness&quot; and creative uses, because Gurps 4e has a far better system for balancing those. So, for instance, a Lasombra gets &quot;Shadow Powers&quot;, and from that they only need to spend points choosing the abilities they desire - instead of fixed levels 1 to 5 powers. It also means each vampire is somewhat unique, even if they have some shared themes for their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T23:17:13-07:00","id":1489839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1489783#post1489783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was one time my group tried converting V:tM to use the Lone Wolf Multiplayer system. This was a simple RPG system by Mongoose Publishing extrapolated from the Lone Wolf choose your own adventure books by Joe Dever.<br /> <br /> The LWM system basically runs off a single D10, a combat chart, a combat skill base number, and an Endurance score (hit points). Rather than having XP you just gain one new ability after an adventure. Rather than seeing if you make a roll or not, if you have the stats, you succeed. But if you don't have the stats, you fail. The ST adjusts the outcome accordingly, though may have you do a roll occasionally.<br /> <br /> On the plus side this made combats so much less of a slog to get through. Rather than figuring out difficulty or number of actions or armor soak, you just take your base Combat Skill and adjust it with any applicable modifiers and compare the adjusted CS number to the opponents adjusted number on the combat chart and roll a single D10, the roll is then looked up on the chart with the results all precalculated.<br /> <br /> The downside is that if you really were invested in the mechanical crunch of the D10 system, this meant your build got boiled down to a very simplified form. Rather than geeking out to Celerity giving you X number of additional actions, it just gave you say a +2 on your Combat Skill and in narrative moments would give you different options considering how fast you could move.<br /> <br /> One interesting thing is that drove home the vampire angle with this system is that there wasn't a Blood Pool per se. Your Endurance Score which functioned as your health levels pulled double duty as your Blood Pool to activate the most powerful of abilities. Thus to using your best powers was a double edged sword, and to heal you had to feed.<br /> <br /> It was fun to play with and in my opinion gave more of a sense of progression than most Storyteller system games, but it was a system that needed far more refinement to make a full port of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Did the use of Endurance create a bit of a XP tax, so to speak?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T23:18:10-07:00","id":1489840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1489784#post1489784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GURPS VtM is for Gurps 3e. Since I much rather prefer Gurps 4e, I have adapted it for the 4e.<br /> <br /> Since Gurps 4e also allows for a lot more flexibilization, I nuked a lot of things from VtM, in particular the Disciplines mechanics. I use the system of powers for Gurps to design their &quot;disciplines&quot;, and in my modest opinion, it's a huge improvement. The powers now are much more balanced and much better suitable for &quot;uniqueness&quot; and creative uses, because Gurps 4e has a far better system for balancing those. So, for instance, a Lasombra gets &quot;Shadow Powers&quot;, and from that they only need to spend points choosing the abilities they desire - instead of fixed levels 1 to 5 powers. It also means each vampire is somewhat unique, even if they have some shared themes for their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does it handle generation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T00:14:44-07:00","id":1489848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1489839#post1489839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. Did the use of Endurance create a bit of a XP tax, so to speak?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Endurance score had a permanent number, lets say 25. If you take Fortitude you could ignore damage from certain sources, and it adds 5 endurance points to your functional total. If you wore body armor each piece added a point or two of Endurance. Each hit you take in combat cuts down your total, once you hit zero you are dead or in torpor. Activate multiple actions with Celerity by spending what is functionally your health levels balances its combat power, but you get non-endurance cost benefits as well.<br /> <br /> At the end of an adventure or mini-story you could just pick one new thing, rather than buying a score in Empathy or Awareness, you just gained the whole trait. So rather than grinding XP you just get say Stealth 5. The flip side is that since the mechanics are gutted of their granularity, the power creep doesn't happen the way you think it would when you imagine getting a whole ability or discipline maxed at five dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T01:44:47-07:00","id":1489858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1489749#post1489749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there was a d20 system by Monte Cook for &quot;world of darkness&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's not VtM. It is a completely different setting.<br /> <br /> And I mean it. Alien invaders come to Earth and start twisting reality because they're an inter-dimensional empire. Vampires were Evil ghosts that had been recently gifted by them with new, special bodies, and werewolves were a race from another conquered dimension brought as a part of the invading army, Mages also had something to do with those recent events, everything begun in the 90's and the &quot;Masquerade/Veil&quot; side of things was an admittedly temporary situation as both aliens and governments engaged in secret conspiracies to avoid panic.<br /> <br /> I mean, it is an interesting game. It also had a valid reason to exist. But it was basically a very loose take on the overall concept instead of a setting adaptation. Yes, I have it, but unfortunately there's little there I can use for my actual adaptation.<br /> <br /> \u200bSince <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> mentioned GURPS, I also want to make an M&amp;M 2nd edition one. And while a D&amp;D one would somewhat ditch the idea of Generation as a hard power ceiling (for obvious reasons, and ditching this aspect of the system would make the whole idea pointless), M&amp;M would easily let Generation be linked directly to Power Level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T04:27:32-07:00","id":1489870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1489784#post1489784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GURPS VtM is for Gurps 3e. Since I much rather prefer Gurps 4e, I have adapted it for the 4e.<br /> <br /> Since Gurps 4e also allows for a lot more flexibilization, I nuked a lot of things from VtM, in particular the Disciplines mechanics. I use the system of powers for Gurps to design their &quot;disciplines&quot;, and in my modest opinion, it's a huge improvement. The powers now are much more balanced and much better suitable for &quot;uniqueness&quot; and creative uses, because Gurps 4e has a far better system for balancing those. So, for instance, a Lasombra gets &quot;Shadow Powers&quot;, and from that they only need to spend points choosing the abilities they desire - instead of fixed levels 1 to 5 powers. It also means each vampire is somewhat unique, even if they have some shared themes for their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Gurps 4e, so I'd like to know as much as you're willing to tell us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T09:16:09-07:00","id":1489891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1489840#post1489840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does it handle generation?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1489870#post1489870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Gurps 4e, so I'd like to know as much as you're willing to tell us.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, for those famiar with Gurps, particularly with 4e, everything has a cost in CP (character points).<br /> <br /> Now, there is the book Gurps: Vampire the Maquerade, but that's for Gurps 3e. The book is pretty much fine as it is, and anyone that likes the Gurps system and VtM setting can use it as it is.<br /> <br /> I have however made my own adaptation specifically for Gurps 4e, because I absolutely love how you can taylor make any kind of weird power or ability or very specific trait imaginable.<br /> <br /> In fact, I play ALL WoD games using Gurps 4e mechanics. I have also made adaptations for Mage the Ascension and in the Gurps forums I was publishing my enti\u0155e adaptation of Wraith the Oblivion for Gurps 4e (I must finish that some day... I just got a little bored, but I'll finish it, eventually).<br /> <br /> If any of you would like to see Wraith the Oblivion converted to Gurps 4e, it's here: <a href=\"http://forums.sjgames.com/showthread.php?t=180897\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.sjgames.com/showthread.php?t=180897</a><br /> <br /> It's almost done, all that needs finishing is the rules for haunts, relics, thorns for the Shadows and finally the many powers - althought the &quot;magic abilities&quot; are the easiest part, since it's only a matter of twinking the Advantages from Gurps. And the rules for Specters, but frankly, with what I posted there one can already play if they choose to. Im particularly proud for the rules over the Tempest Navigation that I made. But yes, it's not finished, and it's spread over a forum, so I need to place it in a pdf someday, but it can help to give you an idea on how this can be done.<br /> <br /> I particularly enjoy my adaptation of Mage the Ascension; for those familiar with Gurps Thaumatology, I use &quot;Realm Magic&quot;, which essentially is like the Spheres; the difference however is that the Gurps system allows you to create your own &quot;Spheres&quot; and have them be balanced in terms of XP points.<br /> <br /> This has been absolutely AMAZING for me. Because now yes, the Hermetics have all the 9 Spheres. However, my Dreamspeaker have only 3: Body, Mind and Spirit (Body deals with the &quot;illusions of materialism&quot;, thus it is roughly what in MtA would be Matter, Life and Forces, Mind deals with the &quot;illusions of the senses&quot;, thus it is Correspondence, Time and Entropy - and no, the Hermetic &quot;Mind&quot; Sphere is NOT part of the &quot;Mind Realm&quot; of my Dreamspeakers, and Spirit is the &quot;illusion of the self&quot;, thus is roughly what the Hermetic Spheres of Spirit, Prime and Mind are).<br /> <br /> My Technocrats dont have Correspondence and Time, instead having the Space/Time Sphere, and instead of Matter and Life, they have Biochemistry Sphere. Thus my Technocrats (and Etherites) have 7 Spheres.<br /> <br /> And my VAs have only the Data Sphere; everything for my VAs is Data (and it's a VERY expensive Sphere in terms of XP due to that).<br /> <br /> Besides those awesome changes, I also use &quot;Sub-Spheres&quot;, which are far cheaper. For instance, &quot;Pyromancy&quot;, for my &quot;Fire Mages&quot;, is a Sphere that deals only with Fire Magik. Thus, my Pyromancer can create or control fire, but cant levitate objects. Likewise, my &quot;Winter Witch&quot; can specialize in the &quot;Cryomancy&quot; Sphere, and acquire control over ice and freeze for a much cheaper price than buying the entire Forces Sphere. Or a &quot;Plant Druid&quot; can have only &quot;Plant Sphere&quot; instead of the entirety of Life, or just &quot;Bird Sphere&quot;, and so on so forth.<br /> <br /> So, in the specific case of VtM:<br /> <br /> First of all I have generation be a special kind of UB (Unusual Background). 13th gen is 0 cost, each gen bellow that costs 5 char points (CP) as an UB. So, for example, being of the 9th gen would costs 20 CP.<br /> <br /> I dont usually allow gen bellow 8, but if I did, I would charge exponentially more. So, to be a 8th gen costs 25; instead of charging another 5 points for gen 7, I would charge an extra 10 (so it would be 35 total). For gen 6, an extra 15 (so it would be 50 CP total). For gen 5, extra 20 on top of the anterior (so 70 CP total) and for gen 4, another extra 25 (so 95 CP total). That is of course, if players could even achieve that much, which probably would never happen (with gen 8 being the most).<br /> <br /> On top of this costs which are just an Unusual Background, the characters must also buy their &quot;Blood Pools&quot;. For those familiar with Gurps Powers, this is just ER (Energy Reserve), and it costs just 1 CP per point. The Pool is related to generation, as is in D10 system. At 10 &quot;Blood Pool&quot;, there is, the max amount of Blood you can have, you are at the 13 gen, and that is part of the &quot;Racial Template&quot; of vampires, so you dont pay for it (you already &quot;paid&quot; the points for being a vamp). At 12th gen however, you have a Blood Pool of 11, so you must pay an additional 1CP for having 1 extra in your pool (thus the 12th gen actually costs 6 CP total, 5 for the UB and 1 for the extra Blood Pool).<br /> <br /> At 9th gen you can spend 2 blood per turn, at 8th gen you can spend 3, at 7th is 5, at 6th is 6 and so forth, just like in the D10 system of the WoD, and the pool for 7th gen is 20, 25 blood pool for 6th and so forth, exactly the same.<br /> <br /> Now, human limits of attributes in Gurps are 20. So that's the limits up to gen 8. Now, it must be remembered that 20 in anything is already INSANE for Gurps, and ANY attribute above 16 is highly cinematographic - even Albert Einstein would probably NOT have an IQ above 17, and Bruce Lee hardly had DX above 16.<br /> <br /> For each gen bellow 8, those upper limits increase by 1. So it's 21 max attributes for gen 7, 22 for gen 6, 23 for gen 5, 24 max for gen 4 and finally 25 max attributes for the antes. Those attributes also have the Enhancement +25% to allow skills to default to those above 20; this means that a 3rd gen Ante with 25 IQ can learn how to use a computer in just a few minutes, and be better at it than most experts. It truly is insane.<br /> <br /> I also let Talents go up to 5 (as opposed to 4 which is the norm), and each gen bellow 8th also increases this upper limit by 1 point - thus a Methusa 4th gen can reach Talents 9 and a 3rd Ante can have Talents at 10, which is once again insanely powerful (as it must).<br /> <br /> For the &quot;Disciplines&quot;, althought I play &quot;fast and loose&quot; with them, there are several powers that are leveled, and thus generation determine those upper levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T11:48:56-07:00","id":1489907,"title":"","content":"For &quot;Humanity&quot; and Paths... I actually never liked those. So I use a different system. Gurps actually has every possible Advantages and Disadvantages imaginable, so I have a list of disadvantages that add up like Callous, Sadism, Bloodlust and others, and I use a system of Corruption present in Gurps Horror, so those Disadvantages get added over time, until finally having Bloodlust &quot;always on&quot; - which means being taken by the beast. Im a little busy right now, when I have time I'll give more details","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T12:39:54-07:00","id":1490046,"title":"","content":"Had a thought. That happens sometimes...<br /> <br /> If one made a solid conversion would they be allowed to put on the Storytellers Vault?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T12:55:32-07:00","id":1490049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1490046#post1490046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had a thought. That happens sometimes...<br /> <br /> If one made a solid conversion would they be allowed to put on the Storytellers Vault?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on the system you convert to and, more importantly, what do you describe of it in your work.<br /> <br /> But in principle, yes. If your conversion follows the rules of the Vault and you put nothing in the document that is protected IP or \u2122 of the other game, then it is ok. And by US (and Brazilian, for that matter, but US is what matters here) law, mathematical systems can't be copyrighted themselves, what can be are other aspects of a game.<br /> <br /> Even then, I would recommend careful thought being given towards each one. Make as few references to the other game as possible so you focus exclusively on WoD material and just translating rules. If a system has an SRD document, it is a safe material to use on this work. Beware the rules of places like D&amp;D's DM's Guild as they're special cases just like the Storyteller Vault, so what they let you do there does not applies elsewhere.<br /> <br /> You may also simply approach both companies if you have something you think is worth publication for mutual benefit. While that's tricky, it isn't out of the realm of reason for them to agree, and then you have the leeway they afford you through an actual licensing, but be sure to have an almost finished product to show before trying, or a really solid project.<br /> <br /> And always be extra careful with layout, both of the book and sheets. Layout is a part of \u2122 and copying is considered infringement similar to identity theft, a \u00a9 license isn't the same as a \u2122 use authorization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T08:26:54-07:00","id":1490134,"title":"","content":"I love the mood and style and themes of this game, but I've never liked the mechanics. I did a ground-up mechanical revision of the game. It was designed specifically for VtM... so it's not really an adaptation to another system. But it is another system.<br /> <br /> Mpst recent version available here: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/o4etwz833sre8rw/Degeneration%20v175%206-2022%20-%20PROOFED%20FINAL2.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/o4etwz833s...INAL2.pdf?dl=0</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T10:58:17-07:00","id":1490153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1490134#post1490134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the mood and style and themes of this game, but I've never liked the mechanics. I did a ground-up mechanical revision of the game. It was designed specifically for VtM... so it's not really an adaptation to another system. But it is another system.<br /> <br /> Mpst recent version available here: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/o4etwz833sre8rw/Degeneration%20v175%206-2022%20-%20PROOFED%20FINAL2.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/o4etwz833s...INAL2.pdf?dl=0</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting. You decided to jettison the Ravnos entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T19:24:21-07:00","id":1490337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489575-vtm-but-in-different-systems?p=1490153#post1490153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting. You decided to jettison the Ravnos entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. I crossed them with Gargoyles and Nagaraja and made them into a highly regional clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}